      "finding": "Nested enqueue could write reentry failure before complete new-holder/output alias admission; constructor could similarly fault busy scratch before capability/budget refusal.",
      "resolution": "Complete pure inputs admission now precedes enqueue writable reentry; capability/control budget precede constructor writable busy latch. Genuine nested holder-output alias returns INVALID and outer enqueue succeeds with holder retained; actual allocator low-budget nested open returns CAPACITY and outer open succeeds. Service/key output checks also precede writable reentry.",
      "source": "src/core/mixed_scheduled_readers.c:109,212,362,393,417",
