    }
  ],
  "state_machine_review": [
    "One bounded queue allocation includes full private command/readers/span admission scratch; full queried external workspace capacity/alignment and declared allocator/backend contexts are checked before writes or callbacks. Known allocation aliases are refused without treating them as fresh ownership.",
    "Pure admission guards complete current input/output, command holder, each new exclusive reader holder and full declared CPU spans. Shared immutable sample/cache data is permitted only with separate genuine pins; declarations cannot prove residency/provenance.",
    "Strict frame ordering, unique route/slot, typed Paula signed8 geometry and numeric AmiGUS cache/address/format/loop bounds are validated before holder callbacks. Card addresses are never cast to CPU spans.",
    "Original epoch/frequency/rate yields one common [first,last) window. One actual clock read and at most one whole paired submit occur per explicit publication; no two-route immediate wrapper, rebasing, catch-up or automatic retry.",
    "Independent command detach proves only command quiet. Exact full reader retirement is separate and releases only when every command reference is gone. Replacement closes stale permission without freeing old readers. CONTROL and STOP require original positive ACTIVE/ADOPTED keys.",
    "Confirmed submit0 keeps ownership local/unpublished for explicit original-window retry. Uncertain publication, late/regressed clock, stale controls and callback reentry retain possible readers and latch failure; later exact independent proofs can drain safely.",
    "Malformed envelopes retain their own domains. Valid quiet envelopes with invalid classification drain only their exact domain, mark terminal valid0, preserve output and return BACKEND. Honest partial issue never invents no-effect or reader retirement evidence.",
    "NULL receipt output explicitly drains. Local stop only drops unpublished domains and closes future publication; no musical STOP or hardware quiet is inferred.",
    "Close refuses held command/readers, invokes only final ordinary allocator release once clear, consumes slot to NULL before release callback, and safely permits terminal NULL-slot close even after former borrowed inputs/config/workspace expire. Final release reentry may return0 after consumed NULL; caller must not reuse freed queue."
  ],
